\v 21 and I'll¦290005 put your robe and sash¦290007 on him, and give him the authority¦290009 \add ≈that you had\add*. He'll be like a father¦290014 to those who live in Yerushalem¦290016 \add (Jerusalem)\add* and \add right across\add* Yehudah¦290018 \add (Judah)\add*.
\v 22 Then I'll¦290020 place the key to David's¦290024 house¦290022 on his shoulder¦290027 and he'll open \add <the door\add* that no one will be able to shut. Then he'll shut it, and no one will be able to open it.\x + \xo 22:22: \xt Rev 3:7.\x*
\v 23 I'll¦290035 fasten him¦290035 in, like a peg into something solid, and¦290039 he'll become a \add ≈wonderful throne\add* for his father's¦290043 house¦290042.
