\q1 will be like a \add very\add* early¦291413 fig¦291413 before¦291415 summer¦291416.
\q1 The \add >ones\add* who see¦291418 it \add ≈will grab it and\add* swallow¦291423 it.
\p
\v 5 \add ≈At that time,\add* Commander-in-chief Yahweh¦291429 will become¦291428 a beautiful¦291432 crown¦291431,
\q1 ≈and¦291433 a splendid¦291434 diadem¦291433 for the remnant¦291435 of his people¦291436,
\q1
\v 6 and a spirit¦291438 of justice¦291439 for \add ≈those who need judgements¦291443\add*,
\q1 and strength¦291444 for those who turn¦291445 the battle¦291446 back at the \add #gates\add*.
\s1 Yehudah's drunken prophets
\rem /s1 Isaiah and the Drunken Prophets of Judah
\p
\v 7 Even those reeled from wine
\q1 and stagger from strong drink.
\q1 Priest and prophet¦291458 reeled from the strong drink,
\q1 and they were confused¦291461 by from the wine.
\q1 They staggered from the strong drink—
\q1 reeling in vision¦291470, they stagger in \add ≈indecision\add*.
\q1
\v 8 \add ≈Indeed,\add* all their tables¦291477 are \add ≈covered with\add* vomit¦291479—
\q1 ≈\add ≈there's no place without\add* filth¦291480.
\p
\v 9 Who will he teach¦291488 knowledge¦291489 \add <to\add*,
\q1 ≈and who will he get to understand¦291493 the message¦291494?
\q1 Those who've been weaned¦291495 from milk¦291496—
\q1 ≈who've already been taken off the breasts¦291498.
\p
\v 10 Because it's ‘command to command to command, line to line to line, a little there, a little there’.\f + \fr 28:10 \ft The Hebrew for this verse (and v13) includes ‘tsav latsav, tsav latsav, kav lakav, kav lakav,’ etc., suggesting that it might possibly have been intended as drunken gibberish.\f*
\p
\v 11 \add ≈Indeed,\add* with stammering¦291515 lips and foreign language¦291517,
\q1 he will speak¦291519 to this people¦291522 \add group\add*\x + \xo 28:11-12: \xt 1Cor 14:21.\x*
\q1
\v 12 telling them, ‘This is the resting¦291530 \add >place\add* \add where\add* the weary¦291532 \add >ones\add* can rest’,
\q1 ≈and, ‘This is the place for refreshing’.
\q1 \add ≈but¦291533\add* they weren't willing¦291536 to listen¦291537.
\q1
\v 13 So¦291539 Yahweh's¦291543 message¦291541 to them,
\q1 ‘command to command to command, line to line to line, a little there, a little there’,
\q1 so they can go, \add ≈but¦291539\add* they'll stumble¦291558 backwards¦291559 and will be broken¦291560,
\q1 \add ≈plus¦291558\add* they'll become trapped and will be captured¦291562.
\s1 A vital foundation for Tsiyyon/Zion
\rem /s1 A Cornerstone for Zion
\p
\v 14 Therefore, listen¦291566 to Yahweh's¦291569 message¦291567,
\q1 you people \add ≈who are always mocking\add*,
\q1 you rulers¦291572 of the people \add ≈there\add* in Yerushalem¦291576,
\q1
\v 15 because you've all said¦291579, “We've come¦291598 to an agreement¦291589 with death¦291584,
\q1 ≈and we have an understanding with the grave.
\q1 When the overwhelming scourge¦291590 goes past,
\q1 it won't¦291597 \add ≈bother\add* us because we've made lies our shelter,
\q1 ≈and we hide in deception¦291603.”
\q1
\v 16 Therefore, my master¦291610 Yahweh¦291610 says:
\q1 Look, I've put a \add foundation\add* stone \add in place\add* in Tsiyyon¦291614—\add *one\add* that's been tested.
\q1 \add ≡It's a\add* valuable cornerstone¦291618—a reliable foundation.
\q1 Anyone¦291622 who trusts¦291622 \add in it\add* won't¦291623 \add have to\add* \add ≈rush away\add*.\x + \xo 28:16: \xt Rom 9:33; 10:11; 1Pe 2:6.\x*
\q1
\v 17 Then¦291626 I'll¦291626 make justice¦291627 into a measuring¦291628 stick,
\q1 and righteous¦291629 into a levelling¦291630 tool.
\q1 Hail will sweep¦291631 away the shelter¦291635 of lies,
\q1 and \add ≈floods\add* will drown the hiding place.\x + \xo 28:17b: \xt 28:15b.\x*
\q1
\v 18 Then¦291639 your agreement¦291644 with death¦291643 will be dissolved,
\q1 ≈and¦291639 your understanding with the grave \add ≈will collapse\add*.
\q1 When¦291639 the overwhelming scourge¦291650 comes past,
\q1 →you'll all be overwhelmed by it.\x + \xo 28:18: \xt 28:15.\x*
\q1
\v 19 When it comes past, it'll take¦291660 you all
\q1 because¦291662 it'll come past morning by morning, \add and\add* day¦291667 and night¦291668.
\p Understanding the message¦291674 will bring only terror¦291672,
\q1
\v 20 because the bed¦291679 is too short¦291678 for stretching¦291680 yourself out on,
\q1 ≈and¦291681 the woven¦291681 \add blanket\add* is too narrow¦291682 to wrap¦291683 around you.
\q1
\v 21 Yahweh¦291690 will \add ≈take action like he did\add* at Mt¦291686. Peratsim.\x + \xo 28:21: \xt 2Sa 5:20, 1Ch 14:11.\x*
\q1 ≈He'll \add ≈stir himself up like he did\add* in Giveon valley¦291691\x + \xo 28:21: \xt Josh 10:10-12.\x*
\q1 to do his work—his special work.
\q1 ≈To perform his task—his special task.
\v 22 \add ≈So¦291703\add* now, don't¦291704 show yourselves¦291706 to be mockers¦291706
\q1 in case your \add ≈chains become¦291709 heavier\add*,
\q1 because¦291711 I've¦291715 heard¦291715 from my master¦291717, Commander-in-chief Yahweh¦291717
\q1 about complete¦291713 destruction¦291713 and¦291703 \add ≈the rest\add* that's been determined¦291714 against the entire¦291722 land.
\s1 The wisdom of God
\rem /s1 God's Wisdom
\p
\v 23 \add ≈Listen carefully\add* to \add ≈what I say\add*.
\q1 ≈Pay attention¦291729 \add ≈to my words\add*.
\q1
\v 24 Does a \add ≈farmer spend all day¦291734 ploughing and not sow anything\add*?
\q1 ≈Does he \add just continue\add* to \add ≈break up\add* and harrow¦291739 his land?
\q1
\v 25 Doesn't he level¦291745 its surface¦291746 and scatter¦291747 fennel and sow cumin,
\q1 ≈and put the wheat¦291752 in rows and the barley¦291754 in plots, and spelt¦291756 \add around\add* the border¦291757?
\q1
\v 26 \add ≈Yes,\add* his god¦291761 instructs¦291759 him,
\q1 ≈he teaches¦291762 him to \add ≈make good decisions\add*.
\q1
\v 27 Fennel isn't¦291765 threshed with a threshing board,
\q1 ≈nor is a cart wheel¦291769 rolled over cumin,
\q1 but¦291769 rather, fennel is beaten¦291777 with a stick,
\q1 ≈and cumin with a rod.
\q1
\v 28 \add Grain for\add* bread¦291782 \add ≈must be ground\add* because¦291784 anyone¦291788 threshing¦291787 it doesn't \add ≈keep at it\add* forever¦291786.
\q1 He \add ≈can run his cart wheel¦291790 over it\add* and his horses¦291792 don't¦291785 crush¦291783 it.
\q1
\v 29 That too comes from Commander-in-chief Yahweh¦291801
\q1 who \add ≈gives good advice\add*—he has great¦291806 wisdom¦291807.
\c 29
